<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">company inventory</ansi>

One screen for everything your company carries.

  <ansi fg="command">company inventory</ansi> (or <ansi fg="command">company inv</ansi>)

It shows:

  - The company's load against its capacity, and how much of that the
    horses carry (<ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>).
  - Each member in turn, you first: the weight of what they wear and
    carry, the pack that counts toward their share, what they're
    wearing, and what they're carrying. A partly used item shows its
    uses left, like <ansi fg="yellow">waterskin (3 of 5)</ansi>.
  - A fallen companion, whose gear stays with the body until they're
    raised (<ansi fg="command">help resurrect</ansi>).
  - Your horses and their saddles (<ansi fg="command">help mount</ansi>).
  - The shared cargo and its weight.

For one companion in full, type <ansi fg="command">company gear [member]</ansi>; for the load and
capacity split, <ansi fg="command">cargo</ansi>.

In the web client, this is the Company tab's Inventory, where clicking an
item sends these commands for you (<ansi fg="command">help webclient</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help mount</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company meal</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help inventory</ansi>.
